What will the console print when comparing String pool literals vs `new String()` objects?

```java
String s1 = "Computer";
String s2 = "Computer";
String s3 = new String("Computer");
System.out.print((s1 == s2) + " " + (s1 == s3) + " " + s1.equals(s3));
```

Analyze the following string code. What will be printed to the console?

```java
String word = "Java";
word.concat(" Programming");
System.out.println(word);
```

What is the output of the following array processing code?

```java
